# Line-ending policy for byte-exact artifacts.
#
# Two kinds of file in this repository are verified by SHA-256 at runtime, so
# a single changed byte is a failure by design:
#
#   * the pinned official reference, whose exact bytes are recorded in
#     vendor/technocore-reference/SHA256SUMS;
#   * the conformance vector bundle, whose digest is pinned in
#     technocore_conform/selftest.py and checked by the runtime self-test.
#
# Git's `core.autocrlf` is `true` by default on Windows - this product's only
# supported platform - which rewrites LF to CRLF *on checkout*. The blobs in
# the repository stay correct, but every working tree gets different bytes,
# and both integrity checks then fail on a fresh clone. The conformance
# self-test fails closed, so the write gate shuts and the whole feature is
# dead on a machine that did nothing wrong.
#
# `-text` disables all line-ending conversion for these paths. It is scoped
# deliberately narrowly: everything else keeps the repository's existing
# behaviour, because only these files have their bytes pinned.

vendor/technocore-reference/** -text
packages/technocore-conform/src/technocore_conform/vectors/*.json -text
